  "reed_hooks_full": {
    "speaker": "Coat Hooks",
    "start": [
      {
        "node": "look"
      }
    ],
    "nodes": {
      "look": {
        "lines": [
          "PARFITT, ROWE, DIMMOCK, LOVEDAY, SKEAT. Five coats on five hooks. Four are wet at the hems.",
          "The fifth is dry. It was dry when I lifted it off the post, too. Somebody's gone over SKEAT in pencil since, to make it darker."
        ]
      }
    }
  },
  "reed_bundles": {
    "speaker": "Cut Reed",
    "start": [
      {
        "node": "look"
      }
    ],
    "nodes": {
      "look": {
        "lines": [
          "Three bundles of reed for thatch, tied twice round, stacked by the fire for Castle to send for.",
          "I carried every one of them, and they're lighter than they looked out in the beds."
        ]
      }
    }
  },
  "eel_cutter": {
    "speaker": "A Reedcutter",
    "start": [
      {
        "node": "a"
      }
    ],
    "nodes": {
      "a": {
        "lines": [
          "He doesn't look up, and he doesn't stop cutting. \"Rats are down, so the eels are up. Reed doesn't know either way. You cut it at the knee and it comes again.\"",
          "\"You'll be the one Mrs Fludd keeps on about. She keeps on about everybody. She'll have told you we don't talk.\" He goes back to the reed."
        ]
      }
    }
  },
  "eel_sign": {
    "speaker": "Board",
    "start": [
      {
        "node": "read"
      }
    ],
    "nodes": {
      "read": {
        "lines": [
          "THE EEL BEDS. CASTLE REED. CUTTERS ONLY PAST THIS BOARD.",
          "Under it, on a newer plank: BEDS CLOSED. Under that, in chalk, smaller, by somebody who wasn't sure they should: rats."
        ]
      }
    }
  },
  "still_sign": {
    "speaker": "Notice",
    "start": [
      {
        "node": "read"
      }
    ],
    "nodes": {
      "read": {
        "lines": [
          "CASTLE RURAL DISTRICT COUNCIL. THE STILL POOL. NO BOATS. NO BATHING. NO MOORING.",
          "Under it, in pencil: S. moored here anyway, every day. Somebody's written a date after it and rubbed it out with a wet thumb."
        ]
      }
    }
  },
  "still_post": {
    "speaker": "Mooring Post",
    "start": [
      {
        "node": "look"
      }
    ],
    "nodes": {
      "look": {
        "lines": [
          "A post driven into the bank, a rope still knotted round it and cut off a hand's width down. The cut's clean.",
          "When I step up to it, the water round the post doesn't move at all."
        ]
      }
    }
  },
  "garden_sign": {
    "speaker": "Gate",
    "start": [
      {
        "node": "read"
      }
    ],
    "nodes": {
      "read": {
        "lines": [
          "MOTHER'S GARDEN. PLEASE KEEP TO THE PATHS. PLEASE CLOSE THE GATE BEHIND YOU.",
          "There's no gate, only the two posts. There aren't any paths. The board's had a new coat of paint this year, and the drips are still on the back."
        ]
      }
    }
  },
